Z||000000||bcwawright||05-20-2001||07:13 PM||||I have a 88GT(2.8) and I have a new 196degree fan switch. I replaced the thermostat with no problem. I can't find the location of the fan switch....there is a sensor below the thermostat neck that is on the engine block and I disconnected the wire and it is a 2 pin plug......if this is the fan /temp sensor I've got problems because the sensor I have is set up for a single pin plugin.<BR>Any help would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thanks<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-20-2001||07:48 PM||||The sensor that is on the t-stat neck is for the temp gauge and ECM.  The fan switch has a single wire connector, and should have a green/white wire connected to it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
